    {
      "confidence": "high",
      "field": "entry",
      "id": "A-009",
      "materiality": "high",
      "reason": "stated in spec.yaml",
      "section": "intent",
      "source": "user",
      "user_confirmed": true,
      "value": [
        "Bars are 5m, open-time stamped, IST; a bar is completed at its open time plus 5 minutes and every rule below reads completed bars only",
        "Session VWAP and SD reset each session and accumulate from the 09:15 bar; typical price tp = (High + Low + Close) / 3; VWAP = sum(volume x tp) / sum(volume); SD = sqrt(max(sum(volume x tp^2) / sum(volume) - VWAP^2, 0)); bands are VWAP +/- 2.0 x SD; every value is as of the close of the bar it belongs to, including that bar",
        "EMA9 of close and Wilder ATR14 on 5m bars run continuously across eligible sessions; an excluded session contributes no observation and does not reset them",
        "The 15m series is built from the 5m bars of each eligible session in fixed blocks of three starting at 09:15 (09:15, 09:30, ..., 15:00), so a session has 24 15m bars; a 15m bar is completed at its open time plus 15 minutes; ADX14, EMA20 and Wilder ATR14 on 15m run continuously across eligible sessions with no reset",
        "Regime is valid when, on the latest completed 15m bar whose close is at or before the decision bar's close, ADX14 <= 22 and abs(EMA20[t] - EMA20[t-4]) <= 0.25 x ATR14_15m[t], where t-4 is four completed 15m bars earlier",
        "Warm-up - a symbol generates no signal until at least 100 completed 15m bars from eligible sessions exist for it, counted from its first eligible observation in the dataset",
        "Long arming - a completed 5m bar e arms a long setup when Low[e] <= lower band[e] and (VWAP[e] - Low[e]) / ATR14_5m[e] >= 0.75; the extreme is Low[e]",
        "While armed, each later completed bar k is evaluated in this order - (1) if Low[k] < extreme, bar k replaces the setup when it passes the same band and 0.75 ATR displacement test (the extreme becomes Low[k], the arm window restarts from k), else the setup is cancelled; (2) if High[k] >= VWAP[k] the setup is cancelled; (3) if Close[k] > EMA9[k] and Close[k] > lower band[k], bar k is a would-be confirmation; it confirms when the symbol is warmed up and the regime is valid at k, else the setup is cancelled and not carried to a later bar",
        "A setup stays armed for at most 6 completed bars after the extreme bar (arm_bars 6) and is cancelled at the entry cutoff; the extreme bar itself cannot confirm",
        "Entry is a market order at the open of the bar after the confirmation bar; the trade is skipped, not entered and exited, when that open is at or above the target or at or below the stop for a long",
        "Short is the mirror image - High[e] >= upper band[e] and (High[e] - VWAP[e]) / ATR14_5m[e] >= 0.75, a higher high replaces or cancels the setup, Low[k] <= VWAP[k] cancels it, confirmation is Close[k] < EMA9[k] and Close[k] < upper band[k] with a valid regime",
        "Execution constraint, not a strategy filter - a confirmation whose stop is closer than 0.5% of the confirmation bar's close is not traded, because the live validator rejects it (risk.min_sl_pct, no per-strategy override); the run counts these as STOP_TOO_TIGHT",
        "The first possible confirmation bar is the 09:15 bar, completed at 09:20, so the first entry fill is at the 09:20 open; the last entry fill is at the 14:15 open",
        "A confirmation consumes only the setup that confirmed, also when the 2-trade cap blocks it; an opposite-side setup keeps its own state until it expires, is cancelled or confirms; when an entry fills, any remaining setup is cancelled, because its extreme is not after the exit bar",
        "One position per symbol at a time; a setup cannot form while a position is open; a re-entry needs a new extreme bar formed after the bar on which the previous trade exited; at most 2 trades per symbol per session, and the run reports how often that cap blocks a confirmation"
      ]
    },
